          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The idea of “ghost” fields was introduced in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Feynman"}> Richard Feynman
              ,
              %em Quantum theory of gravitation
              In: Acta physica polonica. vol 24, 1963, S. 697
          %p and expanded on in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Feynman"} Richard Feynman
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Wheeler"} John Wheeler
              = succeed "," do
                %em Magic without Magic
          %p The BRST formalism originates around
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlo+Becchi"}> Carlo Becchi
                , A. Rouet,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raymond+Stora"} Raymond Stora
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Renormalization of gauge theories
                %strong 98
                287 (1976)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/I.+V.+Tyutin"}> I. V. Tyutin
                , (1975),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gauge Invariance in Field Theory and Statistical Physics in Operator Formalism
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.0580"} arXiv:0812.0580
          %p
            see also the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST"} BRST
          %p A classical standard references for the Lagrangian formalism is
          %ul
            %li#Henneaux90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"}> Marc Henneaux
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lectures on the Antifield-BRST formalism for gauge theories
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0920-5632(90)90647-D"} doi
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/schweigert/ws07/henneaux2.pdf"} pdf
          %p Similarly the bulk of the textbook
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"}> Marc Henneaux
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Teitelboim"} Claudio Teitelboim
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantization+of+Gauge+Systems"} Quantization of Gauge Systems
          %p considers the Hamiltonian formulation. Chapters 17 and 18 are about the Lagrangian (“antifield”) formulation, with section 18.4 devoted to the relation between the two.
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#Jiang95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shuhan+Jiang"}> Shuhan Jiang
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em BRST cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %em Mathematical Structures of Cohomological Field Theories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://nbn-resolving.org//urn:nbn:de:bsz:15-qucosa2-869402"} urn:nbn:de:bsz:15-qucosa2-869402
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/2701230"} spire:2701230
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/files/183359de739dfbf2a8118cd6e5d44700"} pdf
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+current"} conserved current
            of the BRST operator:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Glenn+Barnich"}> Glenn Barnich
              , Laurent Baulieu,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"} Marc Henneaux
              %em BV-BRST Noether theorem
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.19418"}> arXiv:2512.19418
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebroid"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-algebroid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+BRST+complex"} local BRST complex
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            is made manifest in
          %ul
            %li#Barnich10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Glenn+Barnich"}> Glenn Barnich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A note on gauge systems from the point of view of Lie algebroids
              = succeed "," do
                %em XXIX Workshop on Geometric Methods in Physics
              %strong 1307
              7 (2010) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1010.0899"}> arXiv:1010.0899
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.3527427"} doi:/10.1063/1.3527427
          %p Lecture notes from this perspective:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              \: around
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+perturbative+quantum+field+theory#LocalOffShellBRSTComplex"} Ex. 10.28
              in
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} geometry of physics – perturbative quantum field theory
              (2018)
          %p Discussion with more emphasis on the applications to quantum field theory of interest:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , in lecture 3 of:
              %em Dynamics of Quantum Field Theory
              in vol II, starting page 1119, of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"} Pierre Deligne
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"} Pavel Etingof
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kazhdan"} David Kazhdan
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                  , A course for mathematicians
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"}> Yang-Mills theory
            ) in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+AQFT"} perturbative AQFT
            is discussed (for trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            and restricted to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+invariant+observables"} gauge invariant observables
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST-complex"} BRST-complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-formalism"} BV-formalism
            in
          %ul
            %li#Hollands07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Hollands"}> Stefan Hollands
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Renormalized Quantum Yang-Mills Fields in Curved Spacetime
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.3340"} arXiv:0705.3340
            %li#FredenhagenRejzner11a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"}> Klaus Fredenhagen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kasia+Rejzner"} Kasia Rejzner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Batalin-Vilkovisky formalism in the functional approach to classical field theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1101.5112"} arXiv:1101.5112
            %li#FredenhagenRejzner11b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"}> Klaus Fredenhagen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kasia+Rejzner"} Kasia Rejzner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Batalin-Vilkovisky formalism in perturbative algebraic quantum field theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.5232"} arXiv:1110.5232
            %li#Rejzner13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katarzyna+Rejzner"}> Katarzyna Rejzner
                ,
                %em Remarks on local symmetry invariance in perturbative algebraic quantum field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.7037"}> arXiv:1301.7037
                )
            %li#Rejzner13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katarzyna+Rejzner"}> Katarzyna Rejzner
                ,
                %em Remarks on local symmetry invariance in perturbative algebraic quantum field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.7037"}> arXiv:1301.7037
                )
            %li
              %p
                Mojtaba Taslimi Tehrani,
                %em Quantum BRST charge in gauge theories in curved space-time
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.04148"}> arXiv:1703.04148
                )
          %p and surveyed in
          %ul
            %li#Rejzner16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kasia+Rejzner"}> Kasia Rejzner
              , section 7 of
              %em Perturbative algebraic quantum field theory
              Springer 2016
          %p
            With focus on the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"}> José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Takashi+Kimura"} Takashi Kimura
              %em The cohomology of BRST complexes
              (1988) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~jmf/Research/PVBLICATIONS/homol.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/FigueroaKimuar-BRSTCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of the BRST complex of the
            = succeed "/for" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              , p.114 and following of
              %em The definition of conformal field theory
              , preprint, 1988; also in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrike+Tillmann"} Ulrike Tillmann
              (ed.)
              %em Topology, geometry and quantum field theory
              , London Math. Soc. Lect. Note Ser., Vol. 308. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge (2004) 421-577. (
              %a{:href => "https://people.maths.ox.ac.uk/segalg/0521540496txt.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Discussion of the BRST complex for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            (hence with the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            being actually a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebroid"} super Lie algebroid
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"}> José Figueroa-O'Farrill
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Takashi+Kimura"} Takashi Kimura
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The BRST cohomology of the NSR string: vanishing and “-ghost’‘ theorems
                %strong 124
                1 (1989) 105-132. &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104179078"}> euclid:cmp/1104179078
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Belopolsky"}> Alexander Belopolsky
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em De Rham Cohomology of the Supermanifolds and Superstring BRST Cohomology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9609220"} arXiv:hep-th/9609220
          %p
            The perspective on the BRST complex as a formal dual to a space in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-geometry"} dg-geometry
            is relatively clearly stated in section 2 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
              ,
              %em Renormalisation and the Batalin-Vilkovisky formalism
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0706.1533"}> arXiv
              ).
          %p
            For more along these lines see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
          %p
            In relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+de+Rham+cohomology"} equivariant de Rham cohomology
          %ul
            %li#Kalkman93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jaap+Kalkman"}> Jaap Kalkman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em BRST model applied to symplectic geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9308132"} arXiv:hep-th/9308132 (broken)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://cds.cern.ch/record/568522"} cds:9308132
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://cds.cern.ch/record/568522/files/9308132.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jaap+Kalkman"}> Jaap Kalkman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em BRST Model for Equivariant Cohomology and Representatives for the Equivariant Thom Class
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104252784"} euclid:1104252784
          %p
            Making explicit that general observables constitute the functions on the BRST complex regarded as a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-manifold"} dg-manifold
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"}> Anton Kapustin
                , Yi Li:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Open String BRST Cohomology for Generalized Complex Branes
                %strong 9
                (2005) 559-574 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0501071"}> arXiv:hep-th/0501071
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/advances-in-theoretical-and-mathematical-physics/volume-9/issue-4"} euclid
            %li#Jiang23
              %p
                Shuhan Jiang, Def. 4.3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mathematical Structures of Cohomological Field Theories
                %strong 185
                (2023) 104744 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geomphys.2022.104744"}> doi:10.1016/j.geomphys.2022.104744
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.12425"} arXiv:2202.12425
          %h3#history History
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlo+Becchi"}> Carlo Becchi
              ,
              %em BRS “Symmetry”, prehistory and history
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1107.1070"}> arXiv:1107.1070
              )
